<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Felix of Aquitaine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 660–<a href="/years/670">670</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Felix of Aquitaine was a Gallo-Roman nobleman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> who ruled Aquitaine as duke or patrician around the 660s, largely independent of the Merovingian kings. His rule is poorly documented, but he stands at the start of the line of Aquitanian rulers that continued with Lupus and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odo-the-great">Odo the Great</a>.</p></div>
